  @endparblock

  @section credits-index-laboratories Laboratories

  @m_class{m-block m-info m-badge rodin-credit-lab}

  @parblock
  <img src="Images/CFDLab.png" alt="CFD-LAB logo" />
  <h3>Computational Heat and Fluid Flow Lab</h3>

  [CFD-LAB](https://cfdusach.cl/), Universidad de Santiago de Chile.
  Research in computational heat transfer, fluid flow, and fluid–structure
  interaction.
  @endparblock

  @section credits-index-3rd-party Third-party Software

  @subsection credits-index-boost Boost

  Boost libraries are intended to be widely useful, and usable across a broad
  spectrum of applications. The libraries are licensed under the [Boost
  Software License](https://www.boost.org/users/license.html), which is the
  same license Rodin utilizes.

  @par Links
  @parblock
  - https://www.boost.org/
  - https://www.boost.org/users/license.html
  @endparblock

  @subsection credits-index-eigen Eigen

  Eigen is a C++ template library for linear algebra. Eigen provides a wide
  range of mathematical operations, data structures, and algorithms for
  performing linear algebra operations efficiently and with a syntax that
  resembles mathematical notation. It is especially useful for tasks such as
  matrix and vector operations, solving linear systems, eigenvalue problems,
  and more. Eigen is
  [Free Software](https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.html).
  Starting from the 3.1.1 version, it is licensed under the
  [MPL2](https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/),
  which is a simple weak copyleft license. Common questions about the MPL2 are
  answered in the official [MPL2 FAQ](https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/FAQ/).

  @par Links
  @parblock
  - https://eigen.tuxfamily.org/
  - https://eigen.tuxfamily.org/index.php?title=Main_Page#License
  @endparblock

  @subsection credits-index-mmg MMG

  MMG is an open source software for bidimensional and tridimensional surface
  and volume remeshing. It is licensed under the
  [LGPL](https://github.com/MmgTools/mmg/blob/master/LICENSE) and is originally
  based on @cite dapogny2014three .

  @par Links
  @parblock
  - https://www.mmgtools.org/
  @endparblock

  @subsection credits-index-hdf5 HDF5

  [HDF5](https://www.hdfgroup.org/solutions/hdf5/) provides structured binary
  storage for Rodin mesh and field output, including the data referenced by
  XDMF visualization files.

  @subsection credits-index-termcolor termcolor

  [termcolor](https://github.com/ikalnytskyi/termcolor) supplies terminal
  colors for contextual diagnostics in the Alert module.

  @subsection credits-index-petsc PETSc

  [PETSc](https://petsc.org/) supplies the optional distributed algebra,
  linear and nonlinear solvers, and preconditioners used by Rodin's PETSc backend.

  @subsection credits-index-suitesparse SuiteSparse

  [SuiteSparse](https://github.com/DrTimothyAldenDavis/SuiteSparse) supplies
  the optional UMFPACK, CHOLMOD, SPQR, and ParU sparse solver backends.
  Individual components have their own license terms.

  @subsection credits-index-mumps MUMPS

  [MUMPS](https://mumps-solver.org/) provides the optional multifrontal
  sparse direct solver backend.

  @subsection credits-index-scotch Scotch

  [Scotch](https://gitlab.inria.fr/scotch/scotch) provides graph
  partitioning for mesh decomposition through the Scotch module.

  @subsection credits-index-metis METIS

  [METIS](https://github.com/KarypisLab/METIS) provides graph partitioning
  and fill-reducing orderings used by supported sparse solver dependencies.

  @subsection credits-index-mpi MPI implementations

  [MPICH](https://www.mpich.org/) and [Open MPI](https://www.open-mpi.org/)
  provide implementations of the Message Passing Interface used in Rodin's
  distributed builds and continuous integration. Rodin uses MPI through its
  distributed mesh, finite element, and solver paths.

  @subsection credits-index-openmp OpenMP

  [OpenMP](https://www.openmp.org/) provides the compiler and runtime
  interface used by optional shared-memory parallel code paths.

  @subsection credits-index-pybind11 pybind11

  [pybind11](https://pybind11.readthedocs.io/) connects C++ interfaces
  to Python in Rodin's optional Python bindings.

  @section credits-index-development Development and documentation tools

  @subsection credits-index-googletest GoogleTest

  [GoogleTest](https://google.github.io/googletest/) supplies the C++
  testing framework used by Rodin's unit and regression tests.

  @subsection credits-index-benchmark Google Benchmark

  [Google Benchmark](https://github.com/google/benchmark) supplies the
  benchmark framework used to measure Rodin's numerical kernels and
  assembly operations.

  @subsection credits-index-doxygen Doxygen

  [Doxygen](https://www.doxygen.nl/) extracts API declarations and
  documentation from Rodin's C++ sources and documentation pages.

  @subsection credits-index-mcss m.css

  [m.css](https://mcss.mosra.cz/) renders the extracted documentation
  and supplies the site theme and documentation components.

  @subsection credits-index-jinja Jinja

  [Jinja](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/) renders the HTML templates
  used by m.css and Rodin's documentation pages.

  @subsection credits-index-pygments Pygments

  [Pygments](https://pygments.org/) provides syntax highlighting
  for code examples throughout the documentation.

  @subsection credits-index-latex LaTeX and dvisvgm

  [LaTeX](https://www.latex-project.org/) typesets mathematical
  expressions, and [dvisvgm](https://dvisvgm.de/) converts the results
  into SVG images for the documentation.

  @section References

  See the @ref citelist "full reference list" to the scientific papers which have been
  used or provide sources of inspiration for the library.
*/
